# counter harness. One force call is one ASE calculate on the harness Lennard-Jones calculator.
# Local steps are SciPy L-BFGS-B stopped on the ASE maximum atomic force.
# Basin hopping uses the same sampler, rattle, local optimizer, and seed rule as agox/lj38-bh. The confinement cube is 36 Å inside a 48 Å cell. The potential is the harness Lennard-Jones potential, cutoff 40, epsilon 1, sigma 1, no shift. Geometries come from the problem archive. Several of those geometries overlap, and an uncapped L-BFGS-B step puts them on the confinement wall. While the peak atomic force is above 1000, and for at most 40 steps, a local step moves at most 0.2 along that force. The local stop reads the harness force. The box constraint removes the outward part, and a dissociated cluster on the wall would otherwise meet the force tolerance. If L-BFGS-B returns before that stop, at most 25 steps of size min(0.05, 5/peak) follow while the peak force is above 30, and L-BFGS-B starts again, at most four times. A success is an energy at or below the problem reference -397.492331 plus 0.001. The force-call cap is 1000000.
